Post-handshake and teardown record profile, resumed TLS 1.3.

  tool     cmd/postflight
  client   Go crypto/tls (MinVersion 1.3), NOT a browser -- see the caveat below
  date     2026-09-03
  method   full handshake to bank a ticket, reconnect resumed, then hold a
           700ms QUIET READ WINDOW sending nothing, so anything the server
           emits is post-handshake handshake traffic rather than a response.
           Then close cleanly and record what each side puts on the wire.

Post-handshake records are all outer type 0x17 in TLS 1.3, so what is reported
is what an observer can actually use: direction, outer type, length, timing.


